1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:26,000
SPEAKERB: So let's put the whole idea together.

2
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:56,000
SPEAKERA: Draw in, squeeze, burn and push out. That's four strokes, in two turns of the crank.

3
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:26,000
SPEAKERB: The squeeze makes it efficient, and knock sets the limit on the squeeze.

4
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:56,000
SPEAKERA: Patented in eighteen sixty-two by a man who never built one, and made to work by Otto in eighteen seventy-six,

5
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:26,000
SPEAKERB: it's still the cycle inside most car engines.

6
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:56,000
SPEAKERB: It's strange to think all of that is happening under the bonnet, every time a car idles.

7
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:26,000
SPEAKERA: At three thousand revolutions a minute, that's two turns and one push, twenty-five times every second.
